<!--
  Our fork of LineageOS/android_hardware_lineage_compat, for one fix.

  WHY
  lineage-24.0 does not build libwfdservice_shim. The module calls
  AudioSystem::setDeviceConnectionState (libwfdservice_shim.cpp:36), and
  AudioSystem moved library between the two platform versions:

    23.2  frameworks/av/media/libaudioclient/Android.bp:116
            AudioSystem.cpp is a src of libaudioclient
    24.0  frameworks/av/media/libaudioclient/Android.bp:157
            AudioSystem.cpp is a src of libaudiobase

  The symbol is no longer exported from libaudioclient, so the link fails:

    ld.lld: error: undefined symbol:
    _ZN7android11AudioSystem24setDeviceConnectionStateE..._audio_format_tb
    >>> referenced by libwfdservice_shim.cpp:36

  Verified against the 24.0 build: exported from libaudiobase.so, absent from
  libaudioclient.so, libaudiofoundation.so and libmedia.so. libaudioclient.so
  does carry DT_NEEDED libaudiobase.so, but the Wl "no undefined symbols" link
  flag means the dependency has to be named directly.

  NOT OUR REGRESSION. Checked upstream lineage-24.0 tip 07768b889b53: still
  broken there. Neoteric-OS carries the same one-line fix in their fork. We are
  among the few devices still building 24.0, so we hit it first.
  libwfdservice_shim is the only module in that tree that references
  AudioSystem, so one line is the whole fix.

  Branch lineage-24.0 (was port/l24-compat-1) is cut from f1d606ca0973 and merged with upstream 07768b889b53, the revision the tree was
  already on, so nothing else in the build changes. Our entire diff against that
  base is one added line in Android.bp.

  The same defect existed in our own copy of this shim, in
  device/samsung/gts4lv-common/shims/libwfdservice, fixed on lineage-24.0 (was port/l24-dt-4).

  Both shims are needed and are not duplicates. This one provides
  WiFiDisplaySession::broadcastWifiDisplayAudioIntent; ours provides
  AudioSystem::setDeviceConnectionState. extract-files.py references both.

  WHY remove-project, and why the name has no LineageOS/ prefix
  This project already exists in the upstream manifest (snippets/lineage.xml:28),
  and repo keeps one shared path table across the main manifest and every file in
  .repo/local_manifests/. Re-declaring the same path is rejected outright:

    error: duplicate path hardware/lineage/compat in .repo/manifest.xml

  so the upstream entry has to be removed before ours is added.

  The name is "android_hardware_lineage_compat", not
  "LineageOS/android_hardware_lineage_compat". repo composes the fetch URL as
  <remote fetch>/<project name>, and the anton remote fetches
  https://github.com/anton-scholten, so keeping the org prefix would ask for
  anton-scholten/LineageOS/android_hardware_lineage_compat, which does not exist:

    fatal: remote error: anton-scholten/LineageOS/android_hardware_lineage_compat
    is not a valid repository name

  This is the same reason gts4lv-common.xml names its projects without an org
  prefix. The global insteadOf rule rewrites the https URL to ssh, so the fetch
  authenticates with the key that already pushes to our other forks.

  TO DO: send a Gerrit change to LineageOS/android_hardware_lineage_compat for
  the same one-line fix. Once it lands, delete this file, run
  `repo sync -c hardware/lineage/compat`, and the project goes back to tracking
  upstream automatically - the upstream entry carries no revision pin.
-->
<manifest>
  <remove-project name="LineageOS/android_hardware_lineage_compat" />

  <project path="hardware/lineage/compat"
           name="android_hardware_lineage_compat"
           remote="anton" revision="lineage-24.0" />
</manifest>